---
import DocLayout from '../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
import { siteName, supportEmail } from '../config/site';
---

<DocLayout
  title={`Terms - ${siteName}`}
  description={`Terms of use for ${siteName}, the free, open source browser-based toolkit.`}
  heading="Terms"
  updated="Last updated September 2026"
>
  <Fragment slot="lead">
    {siteName} is a personal portfolio project, not a company and not a product. No accounts, no payments,
    nothing to cancel. The short version: your files are yours, the tools come with no guarantees, keep
    a backup.
  </Fragment>

  <section>
    <h2>What this is</h2>
    <p>
      Free browser-based file tools, built by one person in their spare time. No team, no support
      desk, no uptime commitment. Using {siteName} means you accept these terms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="flagged">
    <h2>Not for critical or enterprise work</h2>
    <p>
      These tools have not been independently audited, certified, or tested to any professional
      standard. Don't rely on them for regulated, confidential, legal, medical, financial, or
      business-critical documents. Use established software with formal support and compliance
      behind it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Your files</h2>
    <p>
      We claim no ownership or licence over anything you open here, and as of the date above the
      tools run in your browser, so your files are never sent to us (see <a href="/privacy"
        >privacy</a
      >). Always check the output before relying on it. Every tool includes a preview link, so you
      can check the result in your browser before downloading it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>Don't use {siteName} to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Break the law or infringe anyone's rights</li>
      <li>Process files you have no right to process</li>
      <li>Distribute malware or harmful code</li>
      <li>Probe, bypass, or disrupt the site's security</li>
      <li>Scrape or hammer the site with automated requests</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>No warranty or liability</h2>
    <p>
      Provided <strong>"as is"</strong> and <strong>"as available"</strong>, without warranty of any
      kind, including that the site will be free of defects or cannot be compromised. To the maximum
      extent permitted by law, the maintainer is not liable for lost or corrupted files, lost data,
      or any indirect damages, and you cover us for claims arising from your own misuse. If you are
      a consumer, your statutory rights are unaffected.
    </p>
    <p class="aside">If any part of this is unenforceable, the rest still applies.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Open source</h2>
    <p>
      The code is MIT licensed: read it, reuse it, keep the copyright notice. Issues and pull
      requests are welcome, and anything you suggest may be used without payment or credit owed. The
      licence covers the code only, not the {siteName} name or wordmark.
    </p>
    <p>
      The tools also ship other people's open source code to your browser. Those packages keep their
      own licences, listed in full under <a href="/third-party">third-party licences</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      <a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a>. Run as a personal project from India.
    </p>
  </section>
</DocLayout>
